# hairpins as m lines, the B158 as a thin m/d line across its foot with a
# queue of eight tiny cars (Stau), and the Buergelstein's wooded hump G/g/j
# with its m/d limestone cliff and the walkway bolted to it (an o deck line
# on n brackets). Near-layer colours only (no k, w, h, s, F): the hairpins
# are m, not F, because F is a far colour. Opaque from row 112 down
# (hedges G/j), open sky and lake gaps above between the house groups and
# the two hills. Generated by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the
# grid is the source.
